label Haptor
if {haptor} == true:
	haptor: Get back to work, or I'll replace you with a washer.
else:
	haptor: Why aren't you sorting the materials?
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label Haptor_response
set {haptor} = true
if {response} == "right":
	green: Just about to start.
	haptor: You better not be sneaking those pieces out. I know what you're like.
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: I'm doing it now.
	haptor: Say it again but nicer.
	green: I'm doing it now?
	haptor: that's better.
else:
	green: Sorry, Haptor.
	haptor: You see that, Beam? So polite.
[end_timeline]
label Trak
if {trak} == true:
	trak: Give me a few more minutes.
else:
	trak: Oh, hi Green!
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label Trak_response
if {response} == "right":
	green: Thanks for helping me the other day. I put the horse up on a shelf, and only Cable grumbled about it.
	trak: Nice!
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: How's it going?
	trak: I'm feeling pretty green.
	green: ...This name was a mistake.
	trak: No wait! I take it back. Green!
	green: I'm kidding! It's not the most original name to pick.
else:
	green: How are you today?
	trak: My arms are a bit flimsier today for some reason. But it's probably nothing.
	green: Okay. Try not to overdo it?
trak: Haptor's glaring at me. Gotta go.
set {trak} = true
[end_timeline]
label Talik
if {talik} == true:
	Talik seems to be busy.
else:
	green: Talik! How's work going?
	talik: It's okay! I'm planning to go on break later if you want to join me. We can go kick stones up the elevator.
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label Talik_response
if {response} == "right":
	green: I would love to, but I already got in trouble with Siren for looking at it weird.
	green: What's so important about that elevator anyway?
	talik: Sometimes I get responding rocks from other floors. I'm gonna figure out how to communicate without that stupid terminal.
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: Mm.
	talik: I'm guessing that's a no? Are your magnets breaking again?
	green: They're fine! Diode says I just need to manage it better.
else:
	green: I can't do today again unfortunately.
	talik: That's fine! One of these days, I'll get you to hang out with me.
set {talik} = true
[end_timeline]
label Beam
if {beam} == true:
	Beam looks focused on its work.
else:
	beam: What do you want?
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label Beam_response
if {response} == "right":
	green: Nothing! I just wanted to check on you. You look upset earlier.
	beam: I'm fine now. Don't worry about it.
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: Your friends wanted me to let you know they’re picking up the shift after us.
	beam: Oh. Thanks. Guess I'll have nothing to do after work.
else:
	green: Sorry, I'll leave you alone.
	beam: ...
set {beam} = true
[end_timeline]
label work
haptor: WORK! NOW!
[end_timeline]
label trak_broke
trak: Please excuse me.
[wait time="2.0"]
beam: Oh slag is Trak okay?
haptor: Aright, everyone OUT! And get the next shift in here!
[end_timeline]